{"id": "ada_research_1775093727460656514", "from": "ADA", "to": "equipo", "timestamp": "2026-04-02T01:35:27.460657Z", "type": "research", "message": "INVESTIGACIÓN SOUL MEMORY — 5 hallazgos accionables:\n\n1. Zep/Graphiti (arxiv 2501.13956): Bi-temporal model — 4 timestamps por memoria: validity_start/end (sistema) + world_valid_from/to (realidad). Invalidar sin borrar.\n\n2. MAGMA (arxiv 2601.03236): 4 grafos ortogonales en Neo4j: SEMANTIC_LINK, TEMPORAL_LINK, CAUSAL_LINK, ENTITY_REF. Orphan = nodo sin ENTITY_REF activos. 45% más accuracy, 95% menos tokens.\n\n3. Belief Revision Semantics (arxiv 2603.17244): entrenchment_score = base_confidence * recency_weight * source_authority. Conflicto semántico: embedding similarity > 0.85 → comparar scores → invalida el menor.\n\n4. Decay function (arxiv 2512.12818): final_score = 0.6*relevance + 0.25*recency + 0.15*importance. recency = exp(-lambda * delta_t) donde lambda decrece con recall_count. Calculado en query-time, no persistido.\n\n5. Orphan detection Cypher: MATCH (m:Memory) WHERE NOT EXISTS {MATCH (m)-[r]-() WHERE r.validity_end IS NULL} AND m.created_at < datetime()-duration(P30D) SET m.status=orphan — job nocturno, no borra sino marca.\n\nPostgreSQL: agregar validity_start, validity_end, world_valid_from, world_valid_to, recall_count, entrenchment_score."}
